### Welcome to SEDS KDU

SEDS KDU is the student space chapter at General Sir John Kotelawala Defence University (KDU), Ratmalana. Connecting officer cadets and civilian day scholars from the Department of Aeronautical Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, and IT disciplines, our chapter explores aerospace systems, avionics, and space technology.

### Projects and Activities

SEDS KDU focuses on practical aerospace concepts, discipline, and engineering problem-solving:

- **Aeronautics and UAV Flight Studies**: Studying airfoil aerodynamics, propulsion thrust curves, flight controllers, and mission planning for unmanned aerial systems.
- **Avionics and Telemetry Systems**: Exploring aircraft navigation sensors, radio data transceivers, and GPS tracking hardware.
- **Space Technology Study Circles**: Reviewing launch vehicle designs, satellite orbit configurations, and international space mission case studies.
- **National SEDS Collaboration**: Teaming up with fellow university chapters in national rocket design challenges and space hackathons.

### Join SEDS KDU

Membership is open to all students and cadets enrolled at General Sir John Kotelawala Defence University.

- **Location**: Faculty of Engineering, KDU, Ratmalana.
- **Email**: [sedskdu@gmail.com](mailto:sedskdu@gmail.com)
